{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/878038-kote-lo8md-is-the-scarlet-queen-really-associted-with-phoenixes","id":878038,"title":"[KotE / Lo8MD] Is the Scarlet Queen really associted with phoenixes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-29T13:25:18-07:00","id":878038,"title":"[KotE / Lo8MD] Is the Scarlet Queen really associted with phoenixes?","content":"I was reading <i>Land of 8 Million Dreams</i>, and it states, when explaining the various ages to date, that during the second age, Yin and Yang were separated from one another, and that Yang is embodied by the Scarlet Queen, and that Yin is embodied by the Ebon Dragon. So, far this information is no different from what's presented in the <i>Kindred of the East </i>core book. The deviation comes when the book associates the Scarlet Queen with phoenixes and the Ebon Dragon with (duh) dragons. Then throughout the rest of the book it continually refers to dragons and phoenixes like they're the two sides to this coin or what have you.<br /> <br /> Is there any deeper treatment on this, or any other information about phoenixes in the WoD (East or West)? Or is this stuff in <i>Lo8MD</i> just throwaway language?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:57:00-07:00","id":878191,"title":"","content":"Kind of, but just about any references are incredibly inconclusive and circumstantial. Lo8MD followed the lead of something that was going for a perverse reflection for a reason (i.e. the game was about Hungry Dead existing in a perversion of normal existence, so they do things backwards), but is itself not something that goes in for the same themes, so the result is more than a little muddled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T11:53:44-07:00","id":878896,"title":"","content":"I want to say (without really knowing for sure) that <i>Land of Eight Million Dreams</i> was made in that wonky era that had a decent amount of implied and explicit crossover between the World of Darkness and the Age of Sorrows (i.e. <b>Exalted</b>) worlds. This book fits much better with <b>Exalted</b> cosmology than any others, and the <i>hsien</i> portrayal as 'small gods' and whatnot keeps very well to the notions of divinity and fae aspects presented in the Age of Sorrows, particularly with Third Edition's take on it.<br /> <br /> ...The Ebon Dragon (who we met first via <b>Kindred of the East</b>) is the name of a powerful Yozi - think primordial titan trapped in what amounts to hell - in <b>Exalted</b>, but the Scarlet Queen's closest analog in the Age of Sorrows is the puisaant and godlike Scarlet Empress. These two are not the same as the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen of the World of Darkness; rather they are not yet. There've been hints that the Yozi Ebon Dragon is going to marry the Scarlet Empress for undisclosed - but assuredly nefarious - reasons since Second Edition of <b>Exalted</b>...<br /> <br /> Dunno how helpful any of the above is - or more: I KNOW that it's not helpful for the phoenix-specific part. For that, there IS a totem from <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> named Phoenix, and the Chinese <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fenghuang\" target=\"_blank\">feng huang</a></b> can be found in <i>Bygone Bestiary</i>. A heretic dharma called something like Rising Phoenix is presented in <i>Kindred of the East Companion</i>, I think. Only that last one is likely to have connexion to the Scarlet Queen, but I cannot say how much that would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:30:28-07:00","id":878970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/878038-kote-lo8md-is-the-scarlet-queen-really-associted-with-phoenixes?p=878896#post878896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say (without really knowing for sure) that <i>Land of Eight Million Dreams</i> was made in that wonky era that had a decent amount of implied and explicit crossover between the World of Darkness and the Age of Sorrows (i.e. <b>Exalted</b>) worlds. This book fits much better with <b>Exalted</b> cosmology than any others, and the <i>hsien</i> portrayal as 'small gods' and whatnot keeps very well to the notions of divinity and fae aspects presented in the Age of Sorrows, particularly with Third Edition's take on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that fae have nothing to do with small gods in Exalted. The last time someone tried to forge a connection was the pdf-only adventure Disease of an Evil Conscience, and that was vehemently ill-received.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...The Ebon Dragon (who we met first via <b>Kindred of the East</b>) is the name of a powerful Yozi - think primordial titan trapped in what amounts to hell - in <b>Exalted</b>, but the Scarlet Queen's closest analog in the Age of Sorrows is the puisaant and godlike Scarlet Empress. These two are not the same as the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen of the World of Darkness; rather they are not yet. There've been hints that the Yozi Ebon Dragon is going to marry the Scarlet Empress for undisclosed - but assuredly nefarious - reasons since Second Edition of <b>Exalted</b>... </div> </div> </div>The marriage was hinted at as far back as E:tDB back in first edition, but it (and the Ebon Dragon, too) only really became nefarious later in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dunno how helpful any of the above is - or more: I KNOW that it's not helpful for the phoenix-specific part. For that, there IS a totem from <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> named Phoenix, and the Chinese <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fenghuang\" target=\"_blank\">feng huang</a></b> can be found in <i>Bygone Bestiary</i>. A heretic dharma called something like Rising Phoenix is presented in <i>Kindred of the East Companion</i>, I think. Only that last one is likely to have connexion to the Scarlet Queen, but I cannot say how much that would be. </div> </div> </div>I doubt any of those really has a connection to her, honestly. Especially the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:56:16-07:00","id":880383,"title":"","content":"I mean, it sounds like it's pretty open territory. I'm not the sort of ST that feels like absolute 100% adherence to the metaplot and written materials is necessary at all times, however, I typically like to see what's actually written before I forge ahead (if only to make whatever I homebrew gel better with whatever other systems, stories, characters I find down the line). In this case, it sounds about as close to tabula rasa as it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}